.TH "PERCH-ACCOUNT-ADD" "1" "" "perch" "perch manual"
.SH NAME
perch\-account\-add \- create an account
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B perch account add [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Create an account, its primary address, and default mailboxes in one transaction. If \-\-password is omitted, perch prompts on a terminal.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The account is enabled immediately.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config <value>
configuration file (default: ~/.config/perch/perch.yaml)
.TP
.B \-\-email <value>
account email
.TP
.B \-\-name <value>
display name
.TP
.B \-\-password <value>
password (prompted when empty)
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
show help
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
perch account add \-\-email you@example.com \-\-name 'Your Name'
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBperch\fR(1), \fBperch\-account\fR(1)
